.TH WAIT 1
.SH NAME
wait \- await completion of process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wait
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wait until all processes started with
.B &
have completed, and report on
abnormal terminations.
.PP
Because the
.BR wait (2)
system call must be executed in the parent process,
the shell itself executes
.BR wait ,
without creating a new process.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
sh(1)
.SH BUGS
Not all the processes of a 3- or more-stage pipeline are children of the
shell, and thus can't be waited for.
.sp
